#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d81d981f-ab55-5637-bff5-ae47633b0b79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the System Given a Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efda1d7-ed5f-5d23-8225-a7d46a42bfbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302652} {:answer/id #uuid "36388d96-a26c-5e82-9c4f-5f6e6d23e5ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302791} {:answer/id #uuid "3d878ffb-051c-57c1-acd3-b0fb5ad38498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302840} {:answer/id #uuid "6e069788-d1c9-51c4-808a-bad2aab9de3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303130} {:answer/id #uuid "cbeddfdc-a5ac-54ed-94ef-30ac488f8257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36388d96-a26c-5e82-9c4f-5f6e6d23e5ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302791} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7c351da-96ee-57a7-ad19-0d1fa7a32b4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05eed77e-6ddf-5b27-b62c-35f5a73a8482" :question/math-academy-id "q-332692" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aaeba63f6237121fe226eb30e5378d3e93129bb2782b9c8acb8d73ac719676b3.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait for a decoupled system above.\nWhich of the following systems could correspond to the given portrait?" :question/worked-solution "Writing a decoupled system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are parallel to the axes. These correspond to so-called straight-line solutions of the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The tangents along the $x$-axis are pointing away from the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}>0.$\n\n- The tangents along the $y$-axis are pointing toward the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nAmong the options, the only system that satisfies ${\\lambda }_{1}>0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}<0$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166914 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5ee85e-c6ce-5c8e-bb14-d0a32d6810e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Phase Portrait Given a System: Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6095321f-3c3a-5564-bd76-8ac789465110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/63/635e8687fbccc7612f692ec1a1abaa9802bafe9c3773e4b0c058a18813e7249e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391146} {:answer/id #uuid "9f24dea2-7b89-5ce9-93de-ca7b97049c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a5ae215022638430d0c89dddd97c01ae7598b6251bd013ef48ca9771029b8cd6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391147} {:answer/id #uuid "f70a8ce1-5b6e-5473-90f3-bf87bae67685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9816edf7fb99b759361abc4333f3ed0d3676d2c77db2210367466b66837bca8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391148} {:answer/id #uuid "9fcceae6-4fa4-5965-9386-71fc659c0936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c497d1f9dd6cb5bc473bd46ec56c465228408447fb2436b80f16a23b282654b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391149} {:answer/id #uuid "65324022-a078-5bdb-b4aa-e0381dbb7e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4f/4f613e414cdb619a9b09f25a47b7e4cad953440c40d91f876322d7e1cb59b8c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fcceae6-4fa4-5965-9386-71fc659c0936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c497d1f9dd6cb5bc473bd46ec56c465228408447fb2436b80f16a23b282654b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391149} :answer-field/id #uuid "41bd2e0d-7517-5053-bcbd-08e7df5307b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34a4a204-b6f5-559d-8b71-d224e42d358b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333177" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=9x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=9$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=4$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{9t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{9t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{9t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, there are two phase portraits satisfying these conditions:\n\n![](images/99/99d6e9894c7117c5684e17702540d0eb469b6e824381cf2263c843f8f55ee8d8.png)\n\nLet's consider the solutions $x(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{9t}$ and $y(t)={c}_{2}{e}^{4t}$ provided that ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\ne 0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}=\\frac{({c}_{2}{e}^{4t})^{′}}{({c}_{1}{e}^{9t})^{′}}=\\frac{4{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}}{9{c}_{1}{e}^{9t}}=\\frac{4{c}_{2}}{9{c}_{1}}{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ meaning that the tangents to the solution become more and more horizontal as we move away from the origin. This corresponds to the following phase portrait:\n\n![](images/c4/c497d1f9dd6cb5bc473bd46ec56c465228408447fb2436b80f16a23b282654b2.png)"}]}
